      "card_ids": ["C180","C214","C184","C199","C204","C212","C216","C197"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic clearance and metabolic stability records for related 2-amino-4-oxo pyrimidine, diaminopyrimidine, and pyridyl-containing classes show low-to-moderate intrinsic clearance with no high first-pass extraction: epiroprim human hepatocyte CLint 0.6 uL/min/10^6 cells and low human hepatic clearance (C233, C241), trimethoprim in vivo CLint 1-10 ml/min/kg (C247), cotinine first-pass extraction only 4% in rat liver (C230), a folate analog HLM CLint 8.03 uL/min/mg (C261), and O6-benzylguanine predicted hepatic clearance 11.2-12.8 ml/min/kg (C254). These values do not indicate a dominant presystemic metabolic loss for the query class.",
      "card_ids": ["C233","C241","C247","C230","C261","C254"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Additional L6 metabolic stability records reinforce the supportive direction: a 3-indolyl derivative CLint 2.34 ml/min/kg with t1/2 267 min (C259), mouse hepatic microsomal CLint below 0.5 ml/min/g (C268), and 2-amino-4-oxo pyrimidine thioethers with HLM CLint below 14 uL/min/mg (C260, C242, C246). No L6 record provides affirmative evidence of high first-pass extraction for the query's heterocyclic class.",
      "card_ids": ["C259","C268","C260","C242","C246"]
    }
  ],
